{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Young1967-caseG-thin-thick-59L",
  "Source": "L. Young, \"Multilayer Interference Filters with Narrow Stop Bands,\" Appl. Opt. 6, 297-315 (1967). doi:10.1364/AO.6.000297 - Sec. VII pp. 309-311: Eqs. (49)-(50), Table I currents (p. 305), y = 40; Figs. 14 and 15/16",
  "Notes": "Narrow stop-band filter of alternating thin high-index (ZnS) and thick low-index (MgF2) layers, thin-layer phase thicknesses proportional to 40-dB Dolph-Chebyshev currents (30 elements), y = 40\nSpecification: Stop band at theta/90 = 1 (reference_nm), equal-ripple-like passband; thin layers spaced 180 deg centre to centre.\nReported: Fig. 16 (plot only): peak attenuation about 45 dB (transmittance ~3e-5) at theta/90 = 1; ripples computed for theta/90 = 0.5-1.5 only, reflectance ripples between ~0.0005 and 0.002-0.01 rising linearly with frequency; the two centre thin layers are 40 deg thick, each alone giving SWR V = 1.96 (Eqs. 52-53, p. 312), i.e. R = 0.105 for a single 40-deg ZnS layer in MgF2. Second stop band at theta/90 = 2. Recomputed here: centre attenuation 45.34 dB.\nNotes: 59 layers (30 thin + 29 thick). Thin layers (odd i): theta_i = y*I_{(i+1)/2} deg with y = 40 and the 30-element Table I currents (symmetric); thick layers (even i): theta_i = 180 - (theta_{i-1} + theta_{i+1})/2 deg (Eq. 50). Thickness in QWOT = theta/90 at reference_nm (arbitrary 550 nm), rounded to 8 decimals. Phase thicknesses in degrees: 5.532, 174.608, 5.252, 173.63, 7.488, 171.198, 10.116, 168.394, 13.096, 165.274, 16.356, 161.918, 19.808, 158.422, 23.348, 154.902, 26.848, 151.488, 30.176, 148.312, 33.2, 145.502, 35.796, 143.178, 37.848, 141.44, 39.272, 140.364, 40, 140, 40, 140.364, 39.272, 141.44, 37.848, 143.178, 35.796, 145.502, 33.2, 148.312, 30.176, 151.488, 26.848, 154.902, 23.348, 158.422, 19.808, 161.918, 16.356, 165.274, 13.096, 168.394, 10.116, 171.198, 7.488, 173.63, 5.252, 174.608, 5.532. Paper: thick layers n1 = 1.38 or 2.3, thin layers n2 = 2.3 or 1.38 (\"only the ratio 0.6 figured\"); here thin = ZnS 2.3, thick and both end media = MgF2 1.38 (the stack is embedded in the thick-layer medium, Fig. 14). Normal incidence, lossless.\nLayers from Sec. VII pp. 309-311: Eqs. (49)-(50), Table I currents (p. 305), y = 40; Figs. 14 and 15/16; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours 45.34 dB at the centre; paper about 45 dB (Figs. 15-16).",
